WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.464
Today is October 24, 2026.

3
00:00:07.464 --> 00:00:14.878
Overnight, Wall Street closed broadly lower as defensive rotation intensified across all major asset classes.

4
00:00:14.878 --> 00:00:20.638
The Dow Jones Industrial Average led the decline, dropping one point two three percent.

5
00:00:20.638 --> 00:00:26.814
The Standard and Poor's five hundred fell point five two percent to close at seventy-six twenty-three.

6
00:00:26.814 --> 00:00:30.148
The Nasdaq slipped point two one percent.

7
00:00:30.148 --> 00:00:38.358
Technically, the S and P five hundred is testing key support at seventy-five seventy-eight, its one-hundred-twenty-day moving average.

8
00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:46.667
The tech-heavy QQQ ETF posted its second straight weekly decline, struggling below its five-day moving average at seven hundred.

9
00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:54.535
In fixed income, benchmark ten-year Treasury yields settled near five percent, while corporate credit spreads widened sharply.

10
00:00:54.535 --> 00:01:01.361
Crude oil surged toward yearly highs on escalating Middle East tensions, reigniting inflation fears.

11
00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:07.954
Consumer sentiment deteriorated further, with five-year inflation expectations climbing to five percent.

12
00:01:07.954 --> 00:01:15.258
The Federal Reserve meets next Wednesday, with market pricing showing a ninety percent probability of no rate change.

13
00:01:15.258 --> 00:01:21.349
Persistent inflation continues to box policymakers into a corner ahead of November elections.

14
00:01:21.349 --> 00:01:24.878
Institutions face historic positioning strain.

15
00:01:24.878 --> 00:01:32.280
Goldman Sachs reports book-wide short positions hitting the ninety-ninth percentile, with five shorts for every single long.

16
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:40.466
Hedge funds suffered their worst single-day drawdown since the pandemic, setting the stage for a violent short squeeze if catalysts emerge.

17
00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:47.035
Capital continues rotating out of speculative artificial intelligence growth and into defensive cash flows.

18
00:01:47.035 --> 00:01:57.341
OpenAI reduced its targeted valuation from one point four trillion dollars down to one point two five trillion, marking a systematic repricing across private software.

19
00:01:57.341 --> 00:02:03.101
Hyperscalers face a critical capital expenditure trap ahead of third-quarter earnings next week.

20
00:02:03.101 --> 00:02:09.216
If cloud giants cut data center spending, chipmakers face immediate order cancellations.

21
00:02:09.216 --> 00:02:14.902
If they increase spending, deteriorating free cash flows will compress equity multiples.

22
00:02:14.902 --> 00:02:18.505
New cloud computing plays faced aggressive selling.

23
00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:25.258
Heavily shorted names like CoreWeave and Applied Digital saw monthly short interest exceed twenty percent of float.

24
00:02:25.258 --> 00:02:36.753
Meanwhile, overseas semiconductor bellwether SK Hynix fell to a distressed forward price-to-earnings ratio of two times, reflecting deep market fears over future memory oversupply.

25
00:02:36.753 --> 00:02:39.645
Turning to our pivotal equity focus.

26
00:02:39.645 --> 00:02:47.635
Microsoft, trading as M-S-F-T, heads into earnings next Wednesday facing intense scrutiny over Azure cloud growth.

27
00:02:47.635 --> 00:02:55.515
Consensus expects quarterly revenue of ninety point six billion dollars and earnings of four dollars and seventy-two cents per share.

28
00:02:55.515 --> 00:03:03.162
Investors demand Azure growth above forty-five percent to justify capital expenditures climbing toward fifty billion dollars.

29
00:03:03.162 --> 00:03:10.907
Key technical resistance sits at five hundred thirty dollars, with fifty-day moving average support near four hundred ninety-five.

30
00:03:10.907 --> 00:03:16.753
Alphabet, trading as G-O-O-G-L, reports alongside Microsoft next Wednesday.

31
00:03:16.753 --> 00:03:25.969
Street expectations center on one hundred twenty-seven point eight billion dollars in revenue, with capital expenditures projected near two hundred billion dollars.

32
00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:34.768
Rising depreciation costs threaten operating margins, making the two-hundred-day moving average near one hundred sixty-eight dollars critical support.

33
00:03:34.768 --> 00:03:43.138
Bloom Energy, trading as B-E, plunged eleven point two percent overnight, slicing below its two-hundred-day moving average.

34
00:03:43.138 --> 00:03:51.312
Despite doubling revenue to one point two four billion dollars, ballooning accounts receivable turned quarterly free cash flow negative.

35
00:03:51.312 --> 00:03:59.670
Investors must respect technical support at nine dollars and fifty cents, as markets penalize capital-hungry infrastructure providers.

36
00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.677
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

37
00:04:03.677 --> 00:04:07.844
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
